cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use The Council Method, please cite it as below."
title: "The Council Method — multi-model deliberation with a human chair who verifies by execution"
abstract: "A method and a zero-dependency engine for running a council of language models over technical files (code, decisions, research): an independent round, an anonymized debate by rotation, mandatory claim classification, a binding decisions register, a session quorum rule (QUORUM_NON_ATTEINT), and a human chair who settles disputes by execution, never by vote."
authors:
  - name: "Abdelhadi Bouri"
type: software
version: 1.0.0
date-released: 2026-11-20
license: MIT
license-other: "Method and documents: CC BY 4.0 (see LICENSE-METHOD.md)"
keywords:
  - multi-model deliberation
  - llm council
  - code review
  - decision review
  - verification by execution
  - claim classification
